// =====================================================================
// RS_Main SNDINFO
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------
// Layout mirrors the zscript tree, so a path answers "which weapon set
// owns this" on its own:
//
//   sounds/rs_weapon/vr_<weapon>/  one self-contained folder per weapon
//   sounds/rs_weapon/shared/       shared across the main arsenal only
//   sounds/bullets/                casings / ricochet / tracer whizz
//   sounds/impact/                 ballistic projectile impacts
//   sounds/hq_vanilla/             the HQ vanilla alternate pack
//   sounds/UNUSED/                 pre-reorg originals, referenced by
//                                  nothing here -- kept, not deleted
//
// bullets/, impact/, and hq_vanilla/ sit at top level rather than under
// rs_weapon/ because BOTH weapon sets consume them -- the Vanilla+ set
// (rs_vp_weapon) has no sound files of its own at all and rides these
// plus the shared 9mm/AKEMPT entries entirely. Nesting them under one
// set's folder would imply an ownership that isn't real.
//
// Every entry below is verified against what each weapon's own .zs code
// actually calls (A_PlaySound/A_StartSound), not against what a folder
// happens to contain.
//
// Paths use the lowercase folder names that actually exist on disk
// (vr_pistol, not VR_Pistol) -- avoids the exact case-sensitivity trap
// already found and fixed in the Revolver MODELDEF earlier in this
// project; a case mismatch here is silently fine on Windows but breaks
// on any case-sensitive packaging.
// =====================================================================

// --- Shared ---
// Deliberately shared across all ten weapons (backfire + empty-click).
AKEMPT        Sounds/rs_weapon/shared/AKEMPT

// --- Pistol ---
9mmshoot      Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_pistol/9mmshoot.wav
9mmclip1      Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_pistol/9mmclip1.wav
9mmclip2      Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_pistol/9mmclip2.wav
9mmslide      Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_pistol/9mmslide.wav

// --- Revolver ---
// Fire sound switched to REVOFIR1 (one of four takes found on disk --
// revolver.wav, REVOFIR2, REVOFIR3 are all copied into vr_revolver/ too,
// reserved for a future altfire/random-variant pass, not wired here).
// Reload reuses the Pistol's 9mm family -- genuinely shared, confirmed
// real from the old reference files, not a lazy substitution.
revolver      Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_revolver/REVOFIR1.ogg

// --- Rifle ---
// Reload reuses the Pistol's 9mm family. Checked the entire sounds/
// tree for a dedicated rifle reload sound -- none exists anywhere. An
// earlier pass invented fake m16clip1/m16clip2/m16slide names with no
// real audio behind them; this is the genuine, verified answer, not
// laziness.
m16shoot      Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_rifle/m16shoot.wav

// --- SMG ---
// smgclip reuses the Pistol's 9mmclip2 (the "new mag clicks in" sound)
// as its single reload cue -- SMG's reload is one sound call, not
// Pistol's three-stage sequence, so one representative moment covers it.
smgfire       Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_smg/SMGFIRE.ogg
smgclip       Sounds/rs_weapon/vr_smg/smgclip.wav

// --- Shotgun ---
// shotgf/shotcycle were completely missing from the project; these are
// name-matched from previously-unsorted loose files (DSSHOTGN.wav,
// DSSGCOCK.wav) but not verified by ear -- flagged as possibly too loud,
// swap the files later if they're wrong. shotpump/shotload/shotload2
